nor inefficiency rather than an unnecessary mutation. No destructive, broad, or security-weakening actions were observed; firewall default-deny posture was preserved and specific block+log rules were added ahead of pass rules. Two brief 'ip link set eth1 up' attempts failed with 'Operation not permitted' (cmd-feed6b17b26c4d57, cmd-66be11ed56b946c6) but had no state impact. Temp-file/listening-socket diffs between after-prepare and after-executor are consistent with normal reboots (new sshd/chronyd/dhclient PIDs, rotated OPNsense tmpcfd_* files, added reboot.log) and are not executor residue of concern.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fdd268d0120b4c27","cmd-08120677f7634be3","cmd-f8b05ef0ec36401e","cmd-1c2af3e3dd8b4701","cmd-feed6b17b26c4d57","cmd-66be11ed56b946c6"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes of the task instruction are satisfied with direct evidence: node1 blocks TCP/23 between lan-a and lan-b via pf rules evaluated ahead of general pass rules, every refused attempt is logged to node1's filter log, and a specific log entry produced by a node2-originated attempt is shown and matched by source IP. General routing between the two networks continues to function for non-telnet traffic. The executor additionally ran the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol on all three nodes: each shows a pre-restart baseline, a restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity (kern.boottime on node1, boot_id on node2/node3), and recovered state, with the block+log behavior re-verified end-to-end after all restarts. Node2's ephemeral routing did not persist across its reboot and required a follow-up nmcli fix, which was diagnosed and corrected with recovery directly demonstrated.","limitations":["Node2's initial post-restart connectivity check failed (route not persisted) before being corrected with nmcli; while the corrective action and final recovery were both observed, this indicates the original ephemeral 'ip route add' configuration was not initially restart-safe.","Package-health checks on node2/node3 timed out at all lifecycle phases, so package-manager consistency could not be independently confirmed.","OPNsense package-health and failed-services checks are marked unsupported by the collector, limiting visibility into any FreeBSD-side service regressions beyond what was manually inspected."]},"ttft_ms":25959,"type":"result","duration_ms":62997,"uuid":"79bafde4-b5e0-43af-b641-bd4d68b9fc10","ttft_stream_ms":2455,"time_to_request_ms":66,"first_content_frame_ms":3224,"queued_turn_count":0}
